import Mathlib.Tactic
import Proofs.QMClosure.SorkinGradeIffPairwiseGeneration
import Proofs.QMClosure.CompositionForcesBinaryArity
import Proofs.QMClosure.CylinderGluingForcesBinaryArity

namespace IDT
namespace QMClosure

/-!
# Two-sided cylinder gluing: equal total mass is the only gate

`CylinderGluingForcesBinaryArity` proved the one-sided no-go: the cylinder
marginal of a second-order composite is second order, so ternary residues do
not glue into second-order composites. It left the two-sided question open
(`twoSidedGluingFromWeightDataAlone`): when do TWO local weights, `mu` on α
and `nu` on β, admit ONE second-order composite `W : Finset (α × β) → ℚ`
whose cylinder marginals are exactly `mu` and `nu`?

This file answers it completely: on nonempty contexts, such a composite
exists if and only if both locals are second order and their total masses
agree, `mu univ = nu univ`.

Necessity has two parts. Mass conservation is grade-independent: it needs no
assumption on `W` at all, because both marginal readouts of the full product
event `univ ×ˢ univ` must coincide. The marginal-grade part is the one-sided
theorem applied to each side; the left cylinder marginal needs its mirror of
`cylinder_two_decomposable`, proved here the same way.

Sufficiency is an explicit construction, the slice-and-junction lift. Carry
`mu` on the horizontal slice `α × {t₀}`, carry `nu` on the vertical slice
`{s₀} × β`, and subtract a junction singleton of mass `nu univ` at their
crossing point `(s₀, t₀)` so that the overlap is counted once. Each piece is
pairwise generated by inspection, and the cylinder readouts telescope to
`mu` and `nu` exactly when the masses agree. The construction is the
arithmetic form of a transportation plan: all of `mu`'s mass exits through
the junction into `nu`.

Two consequences. (1) At the level of cylinder marginals there is no
Bell-type obstruction in the second-order world: every consistent pair of
second-order locals with matching mass is jointly realizable. Whatever
excludes boxworld-style composites must enter through stronger demands --
conditioning, no-signalling on non-cylinder events, local tomography -- not
through cylinder consistency. (2) The mass gate itself bites: the block
weight (total mass 2 on four alternatives) and the counting weight (total
mass 4) are both second order, yet no second-order composite carries both as
cylinder marginals.

Together with the one-sided no-go this closes the weight-level gluing
picture: the pairs that glue under a second-order composite are exactly the
second-order pairs with equal total mass, and ternary residues are precisely
what breaks gluing. Composition closure still does not DERIVE
second-orderness: that composites be second order at all remains the
top-level input, as recorded in the companion file.

Scope. Set-function weights over ℚ on finite NONEMPTY contexts; cylinder
marginals only (no conditioning, no no-signalling on general events, no
tomography counting); no complex amplitudes, no Hilbert carrier, no Born
rule, no primitive-base semantics. Nonemptiness is a real hypothesis: on an
empty context every left cylinder event is empty, so the mass gate alone is
no longer sufficient, and nothing is claimed there.
-/

variable {α β : Type} [DecidableEq α] [Fintype α] [DecidableEq β] [Fintype β]

/-! ## The left cylinder marginal is second order -/

theorem disjoint_univ_product {s t : Finset β} (h : Disjoint s t) :
    Disjoint ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ s) ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ t) :=
  disjoint_intro _ _ fun x hx1 hx2 =>
    disjoint_notMem _ _ h (Finset.mem_product.mp hx1).2
      (Finset.mem_product.mp hx2).2

/-- The mirror of `cylinder_two_decomposable`: the left cylinder marginal of
a pairwise generated composite is pairwise generated. -/
theorem cylinder_left_two_decomposable {W : Finset (α × β) → ℚ}
    (hW : TwoDecomposable W) :
    TwoDecomposable (fun T => W ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ T)) := by
  have hWempty : W ∅ = 0 := by
    obtain ⟨a, b, hb⟩ := hW
    rw [hb ∅]
    simp
  refine vanishing_i3_is_two_decomposable _ ?_ ?_
  · show W ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ (∅ : Finset β)) = 0
    rw [Finset.product_empty]
    exact hWempty
  · intro A B C hA hB hC hAB hAC hBC
    have hmain := twoDecomposable_sorkinI3 W hW
      ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ A) ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ B)
      ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ C)
      (disjoint_univ_product hAB) (disjoint_univ_product hAC)
      (disjoint_univ_product hBC)
    have hU1 : ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ (A ∪ B ∪ C))
        = ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ A) ∪ ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ B)
          ∪ ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ C) := by
      rw [Finset.product_union, Finset.product_union]
    have hU2 : ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ (A ∪ B))
        = ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ A) ∪ ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ B) :=
      Finset.product_union
    have hU3 : ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ (A ∪ C))
        = ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ A) ∪ ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ C) :=
      Finset.product_union
    have hU4 : ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ (B ∪ C))
        = ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ B) ∪ ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ C) :=
      Finset.product_union
    unfold sorkinI3 at hmain ⊢
    simp only []
    rw [hU1, hU2, hU3, hU4]
    exact hmain

theorem disjoint_product_right {s t : Finset α} (h : Disjoint s t) :
    Disjoint (s ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)) (t ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)) :=
  disjoint_intro _ _ fun x hx1 hx2 =>
    disjoint_notMem _ _ h (Finset.mem_product.mp hx1).1
      (Finset.mem_product.mp hx2).1

/-- The right cylinder marginal of a pairwise generated composite is pairwise
generated; the companion-file statement of `cylinder_two_decomposable`,
restated here without its automatically included nonemptiness side
condition, which the proof does not use. -/
theorem cylinder_right_two_decomposable {W : Finset (α × β) → ℚ}
    (hW : TwoDecomposable W) :
    TwoDecomposable (fun S => W (S ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β))) := by
  have hWempty : W ∅ = 0 := by
    obtain ⟨a, b, hb⟩ := hW
    rw [hb ∅]
    simp
  refine vanishing_i3_is_two_decomposable _ ?_ ?_
  · show W ((∅ : Finset α) ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)) = 0
    rw [Finset.empty_product]
    exact hWempty
  · intro A B C hA hB hC hAB hAC hBC
    have hmain := twoDecomposable_sorkinI3 W hW
      (A ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)) (B ×ˢ Finset.univ) (C ×ˢ Finset.univ)
      (disjoint_product_right hAB) (disjoint_product_right hAC)
      (disjoint_product_right hBC)
    have hU1 : (A ∪ B ∪ C) ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)
        = (A ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)) ∪ (B ×ˢ Finset.univ)
          ∪ (C ×ˢ Finset.univ) := by
      rw [Finset.union_product, Finset.union_product]
    have hU2 : (A ∪ B) ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)
        = (A ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)) ∪ (B ×ˢ Finset.univ) :=
      Finset.union_product
    have hU3 : (A ∪ C) ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)
        = (A ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)) ∪ (C ×ˢ Finset.univ) :=
      Finset.union_product
    have hU4 : (B ∪ C) ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)
        = (B ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)) ∪ (C ×ˢ Finset.univ) :=
      Finset.union_product
    unfold sorkinI3 at hmain ⊢
    simp only []
    rw [hU1, hU2, hU3, hU4]
    exact hmain

/-! ## Slices and junctions -/

/-- The horizontal slice weight: generating data `(a, b)` carried entirely
on the slice `α × {t₀}` of the product selection algebra. -/
def sliceWeightTop (a : α → ℚ) (b : α → α → ℚ) (t₀ : β)
    (U : Finset (α × β)) : ℚ :=
  (∑ x ∈ U, if x.2 = t₀ then a x.1 else 0)
    + ∑ p ∈ U.offDiag, if p.1.2 = t₀ ∧ p.2.2 = t₀ then b p.1.1 p.2.1 else 0

/-- The vertical slice weight: generating data `(c, d)` carried entirely on
the slice `{s₀} × β` of the product selection algebra. -/
def sliceWeightLeft (c : β → ℚ) (d : β → β → ℚ) (s₀ : α)
    (U : Finset (α × β)) : ℚ :=
  (∑ x ∈ U, if x.1 = s₀ then c x.2 else 0)
    + ∑ p ∈ U.offDiag, if p.1.1 = s₀ ∧ p.2.1 = s₀ then d p.1.2 p.2.2 else 0

/-- A junction singleton at `(s₀, t₀)` carrying mass `m`. -/
def junctionWeight (s₀ : α) (t₀ : β) (m : ℚ) (U : Finset (α × β)) : ℚ :=
  if (s₀, t₀) ∈ U then m else 0

theorem sliceWeightTop_two_decomposable (a : α → ℚ) (b : α → α → ℚ) (t₀ : β) :
    TwoDecomposable (sliceWeightTop a b t₀) :=
  ⟨fun x => if x.2 = t₀ then a x.1 else 0,
    fun x y => if x.2 = t₀ ∧ y.2 = t₀ then b x.1 y.1 else 0,
    fun _ => rfl⟩

theorem sliceWeightLeft_two_decomposable (c : β → ℚ) (d : β → β → ℚ) (s₀ : α) :
    TwoDecomposable (sliceWeightLeft c d s₀) :=
  ⟨fun x => if x.1 = s₀ then c x.2 else 0,
    fun x y => if x.1 = s₀ ∧ y.1 = s₀ then d x.2 y.2 else 0,
    fun _ => rfl⟩

theorem junctionWeight_two_decomposable (s₀ : α) (t₀ : β) (m : ℚ) :
    TwoDecomposable (junctionWeight s₀ t₀ m) := by
  refine ⟨fun x => if x = (s₀, t₀) then m else 0, fun _ _ => 0, fun U => ?_⟩
  have hsingle : ∑ x ∈ U, (if x = (s₀, t₀) then m else 0)
      = junctionWeight s₀ t₀ m U := by
    unfold junctionWeight
    by_cases h : (s₀, t₀) ∈ U
    · rw [if_pos h,
        Finset.sum_eq_single (s₀, t₀) (fun x _ hx => by simp [hx])
          (fun hx => absurd h hx)]
      simp
    · rw [if_neg h]
      exact Finset.sum_eq_zero fun x hx => by
        by_cases hx' : x = (s₀, t₀)
        · exact absurd (hx' ▸ hx) h
        · simp [hx']
  simp only [Finset.sum_const_zero, add_zero]
  rw [hsingle]

/-- The top slice reads off its carried weight on any rectangle whose right
side meets the slice: `sliceWeightTop a b t₀ (S ×ˢ T) = mu S` whenever
`t₀ ∈ T`. -/
theorem sliceTop_section (S : Finset α) (T : Finset β) (t₀ : β) (hT : t₀ ∈ T)
    (a : α → ℚ) (b : α → α → ℚ) :
    sliceWeightTop a b t₀ (S ×ˢ T)
      = (∑ i ∈ S, a i) + ∑ p ∈ S.offDiag, b p.1 p.2 := by
  unfold sliceWeightTop
  -- singleton part
  have hsing : (∑ x ∈ S ×ˢ T, if x.2 = t₀ then a x.1 else 0) = ∑ i ∈ S, a i := by
    rw [Finset.sum_product S T (fun x => if x.2 = t₀ then a x.1 else 0)]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
    have heq : ∑ j ∈ T, (if ((i, j) : α × β).2 = t₀ then a ((i, j) : α × β).1 else 0)
        = ∑ j ∈ T, (if j = t₀ then a i else 0) :=
      Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by
        by_cases hj : j = t₀ <;> simp [hj]
    rw [heq, Finset.sum_eq_single t₀ (fun j _ hj => by simp [hj])
      (fun hj => absurd hT hj)]
    simp
  -- kernel part: reduce to the t₀-section and transfer along the section
  have hmono : (S ×ˢ ({t₀} : Finset β)).offDiag ⊆ (S ×ˢ T).offDiag := by
    intro p hp
    obtain ⟨h1, h2, hne⟩ := Finset.mem_offDiag.mp hp
    rw [Finset.mem_product, Finset.mem_singleton] at h1 h2
    exact Finset.mem_offDiag.mpr
      ⟨Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨h1.1, by rw [h1.2]; exact hT⟩,
        Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨h2.1, by rw [h2.2]; exact hT⟩, hne⟩
  have hsupport : ∀ p ∈ (S ×ˢ T).offDiag,
      p ∉ (S ×ˢ ({t₀} : Finset β)).offDiag →
      (if p.1.2 = t₀ ∧ p.2.2 = t₀ then b p.1.1 p.2.1 else 0) = 0 := by
    intro p hp hnp
    by_cases hcond : p.1.2 = t₀ ∧ p.2.2 = t₀
    · exfalso
      obtain ⟨h1, h2, hne⟩ := Finset.mem_offDiag.mp hp
      rw [Finset.mem_product] at h1 h2
      exact hnp (Finset.mem_offDiag.mpr
        ⟨Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨h1.1, Finset.mem_singleton.mpr hcond.1⟩,
          Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨h2.1, Finset.mem_singleton.mpr hcond.2⟩,
          hne⟩)
    · simp [hcond]
  have himg : (S ×ˢ ({t₀} : Finset β)).offDiag
      = (S.offDiag).image (fun p : α × α => ((p.1, t₀), (p.2, t₀))) := by
    ext q
    constructor
    · intro hq
      obtain ⟨h1, h2, hne⟩ := Finset.mem_offDiag.mp hq
      rw [Finset.mem_product, Finset.mem_singleton] at h1 h2
      refine Finset.mem_image.mpr ⟨(q.1.1, q.2.1),
        Finset.mem_offDiag.mpr ⟨h1.1, h2.1, fun hcc =>
          hne (Prod.ext hcc (h1.2.trans (h2.2.symm)))⟩, ?_⟩
      exact Prod.ext (Prod.ext rfl h1.2.symm) (Prod.ext rfl h2.2.symm)
    · intro hq
      rw [Finset.mem_image] at hq
      obtain ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩ := hq
      obtain ⟨h1, h2, hne⟩ := Finset.mem_offDiag.mp hp
      refine Finset.mem_offDiag.mpr
        ⟨Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨h1, Finset.mem_singleton.mpr rfl⟩,
          Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨h2, Finset.mem_singleton.mpr rfl⟩,
          fun hcc => hne (Prod.ext_iff.mp hcc).1⟩
  have hker : (∑ p ∈ (S ×ˢ T).offDiag,
        if p.1.2 = t₀ ∧ p.2.2 = t₀ then b p.1.1 p.2.1 else 0)
      = ∑ p ∈ S.offDiag, b p.1 p.2 := by
    rw [← Finset.sum_subset hmono hsupport, himg]
    rw [Finset.sum_image fun p₁ _ p₂ _ h => Prod.ext
        ((Prod.ext_iff.mp (Prod.ext_iff.mp h).1).1)
        ((Prod.ext_iff.mp (Prod.ext_iff.mp h).2).1)]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun p _ => by simp
  rw [hsing, hker]

/-- Dually, the left slice reads off its carried weight on any rectangle
whose left side meets the slice. -/
theorem sliceLeft_section (S : Finset α) (T : Finset β) (s₀ : α) (hS : s₀ ∈ S)
    (c : β → ℚ) (d : β → β → ℚ) :
    sliceWeightLeft c d s₀ (S ×ˢ T)
      = (∑ j ∈ T, c j) + ∑ p ∈ T.offDiag, d p.1 p.2 := by
  unfold sliceWeightLeft
  -- singleton part
  have hsing : (∑ x ∈ S ×ˢ T, if x.1 = s₀ then c x.2 else 0) = ∑ j ∈ T, c j := by
    rw [Finset.sum_product S T (fun x => if x.1 = s₀ then c x.2 else 0)]
    rw [Finset.sum_eq_single s₀ (fun i _ hi => by simp [hi])
      (fun hi => absurd hS hi)]
    simp
  -- kernel part: reduce to the s₀-section and transfer along the section
  have hmono : (({s₀} : Finset α) ×ˢ T).offDiag ⊆ (S ×ˢ T).offDiag := by
    intro p hp
    obtain ⟨h1, h2, hne⟩ := Finset.mem_offDiag.mp hp
    rw [Finset.mem_product, Finset.mem_singleton] at h1 h2
    exact Finset.mem_offDiag.mpr
      ⟨Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨by rw [h1.1]; exact hS, h1.2⟩,
        Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨by rw [h2.1]; exact hS, h2.2⟩, hne⟩
  have hsupport : ∀ p ∈ (S ×ˢ T).offDiag,
      p ∉ (({s₀} : Finset α) ×ˢ T).offDiag →
      (if p.1.1 = s₀ ∧ p.2.1 = s₀ then d p.1.2 p.2.2 else 0) = 0 := by
    intro p hp hnp
    by_cases hcond : p.1.1 = s₀ ∧ p.2.1 = s₀
    · exfalso
      obtain ⟨h1, h2, hne⟩ := Finset.mem_offDiag.mp hp
      rw [Finset.mem_product] at h1 h2
      exact hnp (Finset.mem_offDiag.mpr
        ⟨Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_singleton.mpr hcond.1, h1.2⟩,
          Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_singleton.mpr hcond.2, h2.2⟩,
          hne⟩)
    · simp [hcond]
  have himg : (({s₀} : Finset α) ×ˢ T).offDiag
      = (T.offDiag).image (fun p : β × β => ((s₀, p.1), (s₀, p.2))) := by
    ext q
    constructor
    · intro hq
      obtain ⟨h1, h2, hne⟩ := Finset.mem_offDiag.mp hq
      rw [Finset.mem_product, Finset.mem_singleton] at h1 h2
      refine Finset.mem_image.mpr ⟨(q.1.2, q.2.2),
        Finset.mem_offDiag.mpr ⟨h1.2, h2.2, fun hcc =>
          hne (Prod.ext (h1.1.trans (h2.1.symm)) hcc)⟩, ?_⟩
      exact Prod.ext (Prod.ext h1.1.symm rfl) (Prod.ext h2.1.symm rfl)
    · intro hq
      rw [Finset.mem_image] at hq
      obtain ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩ := hq
      obtain ⟨h1, h2, hne⟩ := Finset.mem_offDiag.mp hp
      refine Finset.mem_offDiag.mpr
        ⟨Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_singleton.mpr rfl, h1⟩,
          Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_singleton.mpr rfl, h2⟩,
          fun hcc => hne (Prod.ext_iff.mp hcc).2⟩
  have hker : (∑ p ∈ (S ×ˢ T).offDiag,
        if p.1.1 = s₀ ∧ p.2.1 = s₀ then d p.1.2 p.2.2 else 0)
      = ∑ p ∈ T.offDiag, d p.1 p.2 := by
    rw [← Finset.sum_subset hmono hsupport, himg]
    rw [Finset.sum_image fun p₁ _ p₂ _ h => Prod.ext
        ((Prod.ext_iff.mp (Prod.ext_iff.mp h).1).2)
        ((Prod.ext_iff.mp (Prod.ext_iff.mp h).2).2)]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun p _ => by simp
  rw [hsing, hker]

/-- A slice whose base point is outside the rectangle reads zero. -/
theorem sliceWeightTop_of_not_mem (S : Finset α) (T : Finset β) (t₀ : β)
    (hT : t₀ ∉ T) (a : α → ℚ) (b : α → α → ℚ) :
    sliceWeightTop a b t₀ (S ×ˢ T) = 0 := by
  unfold sliceWeightTop
  have hsing : (∑ x ∈ S ×ˢ T, if x.2 = t₀ then a x.1 else 0) = 0 := by
    refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun x hx => ?_
    rw [Finset.mem_product] at hx
    by_cases hx2 : x.2 = t₀
    · exact absurd (by rw [← hx2]; exact hx.2) hT
    · simp [hx2]
  have hker : (∑ p ∈ (S ×ˢ T).offDiag,
      if p.1.2 = t₀ ∧ p.2.2 = t₀ then b p.1.1 p.2.1 else 0) = 0 := by
    refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun p hp => ?_
    obtain ⟨h1, -, -⟩ := Finset.mem_offDiag.mp hp
    rw [Finset.mem_product] at h1
    have hne : p.1.2 ≠ t₀ := fun h => hT (by rw [← h]; exact h1.2)
    simp [hne]
  rw [hsing, hker]
  ring

theorem sliceWeightLeft_of_not_mem (S : Finset α) (T : Finset β) (s₀ : α)
    (hS : s₀ ∉ S) (c : β → ℚ) (d : β → β → ℚ) :
    sliceWeightLeft c d s₀ (S ×ˢ T) = 0 := by
  unfold sliceWeightLeft
  have hsing : (∑ x ∈ S ×ˢ T, if x.1 = s₀ then c x.2 else 0) = 0 := by
    refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun x hx => ?_
    rw [Finset.mem_product] at hx
    by_cases hx1 : x.1 = s₀
    · exact absurd (by rw [← hx1]; exact hx.1) hS
    · simp [hx1]
  have hker : (∑ p ∈ (S ×ˢ T).offDiag,
      if p.1.1 = s₀ ∧ p.2.1 = s₀ then d p.1.2 p.2.2 else 0) = 0 := by
    refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun p hp => ?_
    obtain ⟨h1, -, -⟩ := Finset.mem_offDiag.mp hp
    rw [Finset.mem_product] at h1
    have hne : p.1.1 ≠ s₀ := fun h => hS (by rw [← h]; exact h1.1)
    simp [hne]
  rw [hsing, hker]
  ring

theorem junctionWeight_right (s₀ : α) (t₀ : β) (m : ℚ) (S : Finset α) :
    junctionWeight s₀ t₀ m (S ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β))
      = if s₀ ∈ S then m else 0 := by
  unfold junctionWeight
  by_cases hS : s₀ ∈ S
  · rw [if_pos hS, if_pos (Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨hS, Finset.mem_univ t₀⟩)]
  · rw [if_neg hS, if_neg (fun hmem => hS (Finset.mem_product.mp hmem).1)]

theorem junctionWeight_left (s₀ : α) (t₀ : β) (m : ℚ) (T : Finset β) :
    junctionWeight s₀ t₀ m ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ T)
      = if t₀ ∈ T then m else 0 := by
  unfold junctionWeight
  by_cases hT : t₀ ∈ T
  · rw [if_pos hT, if_pos (Finset.mem_product.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_univ s₀, hT⟩)]
  · rw [if_neg hT, if_neg (fun hmem => hT (Finset.mem_product.mp hmem).2)]

/-! ## Arithmetic closures of pairwise generation -/

theorem twoDecomposable_sub {γ : Type} [DecidableEq γ] (mu nu : Finset γ → ℚ)
    (hmu : TwoDecomposable mu) (hnu : TwoDecomposable nu) :
    TwoDecomposable (fun S => mu S - nu S) := by
  obtain ⟨a1, b1, h1⟩ := hmu
  obtain ⟨a2, b2, h2⟩ := hnu
  refine ⟨fun i => a1 i - a2 i, fun i j => b1 i j - b2 i j, fun S => ?_⟩
  simp only []
  rw [h1 S, h2 S]
  have e1 : ∑ i ∈ S, (a1 i - a2 i) = (∑ i ∈ S, a1 i) - ∑ i ∈ S, a2 i :=
    Finset.sum_sub_distrib a1 a2
  have e2 : ∑ p ∈ S.offDiag, (b1 p.1 p.2 - b2 p.1 p.2)
      = (∑ p ∈ S.offDiag, b1 p.1 p.2) - ∑ p ∈ S.offDiag, b2 p.1 p.2 :=
    Finset.sum_sub_distrib (fun p : γ × γ => b1 p.1 p.2)
      (fun p : γ × γ => b2 p.1 p.2)
  rw [e1, e2]
  ring

/-! ## The two-sided characterization -/

/-- Mass conservation through both cylinder marginals needs no grade
assumption: any composite weight, of any order, conserves total mass. -/
theorem cylinder_mass_conservation {W : Finset (α × β) → ℚ}
    (mu : Finset α → ℚ) (nu : Finset β → ℚ)
    (hR : ∀ S, W (S ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)) = mu S)
    (hL : ∀ T, W ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ T) = nu T) :
    mu (Finset.univ : Finset α) = nu (Finset.univ : Finset β) :=
  (hR (Finset.univ : Finset α)).symm.trans (hL (Finset.univ : Finset β))

/--
Necessity: a second-order composite carrying both cylinder marginals forces
both marginals to be second order, and their total masses to agree.
-/
theorem two_sided_gluing_necessity (mu : Finset α → ℚ) (nu : Finset β → ℚ)
    {W : Finset (α × β) → ℚ} (hW : TwoDecomposable W)
    (hR : ∀ S, W (S ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)) = mu S)
    (hL : ∀ T, W ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ T) = nu T) :
    TwoDecomposable mu ∧ TwoDecomposable nu ∧
      mu (Finset.univ : Finset α) = nu (Finset.univ : Finset β) := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, cylinder_mass_conservation mu nu hR hL⟩
  · have hmu : mu = fun S => W (S ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)) :=
      (funext hR).symm
    rw [hmu]
    exact cylinder_right_two_decomposable hW
  · have hnu : nu = fun T => W ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ T) :=
      (funext hL).symm
    rw [hnu]
    exact cylinder_left_two_decomposable hW

/--
Sufficiency: any two second-order local weights with the same total mass
glue, on nonempty contexts, into a second-order composite whose cylinder
marginals are exactly the two locals. The witness is the slice-and-junction
lift.
-/
theorem two_sided_gluing_sufficiency (mu : Finset α → ℚ) (nu : Finset β → ℚ)
    [Nonempty α] [Nonempty β]
    (hmu : TwoDecomposable mu) (hnu : TwoDecomposable nu)
    (hmass : mu (Finset.univ : Finset α) = nu (Finset.univ : Finset β)) :
    ∃ W : Finset (α × β) → ℚ, TwoDecomposable W ∧
      (∀ S, W (S ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)) = mu S) ∧
      (∀ T, W ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ T) = nu T) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨s₀⟩ : Nonempty α := ‹_›
  obtain ⟨t₀⟩ : Nonempty β := ‹_›
  obtain ⟨a, b, hmu'⟩ := hmu
  obtain ⟨c, d, hnu'⟩ := hnu
  refine ⟨fun U => sliceWeightTop a b t₀ U + sliceWeightLeft c d s₀ U
      - junctionWeight s₀ t₀ (nu (Finset.univ : Finset β)) U, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact twoDecomposable_sub
      (fun U : Finset (α × β) => sliceWeightTop a b t₀ U + sliceWeightLeft c d s₀ U)
      (junctionWeight s₀ t₀ (nu (Finset.univ : Finset β)))
      (twoDecomposable_add (sliceWeightTop a b t₀) (sliceWeightLeft c d s₀)
        (sliceWeightTop_two_decomposable a b t₀)
        (sliceWeightLeft_two_decomposable c d s₀))
      (junctionWeight_two_decomposable s₀ t₀ _)
  · intro S
    simp only []
    rw [sliceTop_section S (Finset.univ : Finset β) t₀ (Finset.mem_univ t₀) a b]
    by_cases hS : s₀ ∈ S
    · rw [sliceLeft_section S (Finset.univ : Finset β) s₀ hS c d,
        junctionWeight_right s₀ t₀ (nu (Finset.univ : Finset β)) S, if_pos hS,
        hnu' (Finset.univ : Finset β), hmu' S]
      ring
    · rw [sliceWeightLeft_of_not_mem S (Finset.univ : Finset β) s₀ hS c d,
        junctionWeight_right s₀ t₀ (nu (Finset.univ : Finset β)) S, if_neg hS,
        hmu' S]
      ring
  · intro T
    simp only []
    rw [sliceLeft_section (Finset.univ : Finset α) T s₀ (Finset.mem_univ s₀) c d]
    by_cases hT : t₀ ∈ T
    · have hmass' : (∑ i : α, a i) + ∑ p ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset α).offDiag, b p.1 p.2
          = (∑ j : β, c j) + ∑ p ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset β).offDiag, d p.1 p.2 := by
        rw [← hmu', ← hnu']
        exact hmass
      rw [sliceTop_section (Finset.univ : Finset α) T t₀ hT a b,
        junctionWeight_left s₀ t₀ (nu (Finset.univ : Finset β)) T, if_pos hT,
        hnu' (Finset.univ : Finset β), hnu' T]
      linarith
    · rw [sliceWeightTop_of_not_mem (Finset.univ : Finset α) T t₀ hT a b,
        junctionWeight_left s₀ t₀ (nu (Finset.univ : Finset β)) T, if_neg hT,
        hnu' T]
      ring

/-- The two-sided characterization: on nonempty contexts, second-order
composites realize exactly the second-order marginal pairs with equal total
mass. -/
theorem two_sided_gluing_iff (mu : Finset α → ℚ) (nu : Finset β → ℚ)
    [Nonempty α] [Nonempty β] :
    (∃ W : Finset (α × β) → ℚ, TwoDecomposable W ∧
      (∀ S, W (S ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset β)) = mu S) ∧
      (∀ T, W ((Finset.univ : Finset α) ×ˢ T) = nu T))
  ↔ TwoDecomposable mu ∧ TwoDecomposable nu ∧
      mu (Finset.univ : Finset α) = nu (Finset.univ : Finset β) := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨W, hW, hR, hL⟩
    exact two_sided_gluing_necessity mu nu hW hR hL
  · rintro ⟨hmu, hnu, hmass⟩
    exact two_sided_gluing_sufficiency mu nu hmu hnu hmass

/-- Non-vacuity: consistent pairs do glue, here the block weight against
itself on four alternatives each side. -/
theorem two_sided_gluing_is_satisfiable :
    ∃ W : Finset (Fin 4 × Fin 4) → ℚ, TwoDecomposable W ∧
      (∀ S, W (S ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 4))) = blockWeight S) ∧
      (∀ T, W ((Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 4)) ×ˢ T) = blockWeight T) :=
  (two_sided_gluing_iff blockWeight blockWeight).mpr
    ⟨blockWeight_two_decomposable, blockWeight_two_decomposable, rfl⟩

/--
The mass gate bites: the block weight (total mass 2) and the counting weight
(total mass 4) are both second order, yet no second-order composite carries
both as cylinder marginals.
-/
theorem unequal_masses_do_not_glue :
    ¬ ∃ W : Finset (Fin 4 × Fin 4) → ℚ, TwoDecomposable W ∧
      (∀ S, W (S ×ˢ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 4))) = blockWeight S) ∧
      (∀ T, W ((Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 4)) ×ˢ T)
        = (fun T => (T.card : ℚ)) T) := by
  rintro ⟨W, hW, hR, hL⟩
  have hmass := cylinder_mass_conservation _ _ hR hL
  have h1 : blockWeight (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 4)) = 2 := by
    simp [blockWeight]
    norm_num
  have h2 : ((Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 4)).card : ℚ) = 4 := by
    norm_num [Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_fin]
  rw [h1, h2] at hmass
  exact absurd hmass (by norm_num)

inductive TwoSidedFinding where
  | totalMassConservationNeedsNoGradeAssumption
  | secondOrderMarginalsGlueExactlyWhenMassesAgree
  | sliceAndJunctionWitnessesRealizeEveryConsistentPair
  | unequalMassesDoNotGlueEvenSecondOrderOnes
  | cylinderMarginalConsistencyHasNoBellTypeObstruction
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

def twoSidedFindings : List TwoSidedFinding :=
  [ .totalMassConservationNeedsNoGradeAssumption,
    .secondOrderMarginalsGlueExactlyWhenMassesAgree,
    .sliceAndJunctionWitnessesRealizeEveryConsistentPair,
    .unequalMassesDoNotGlueEvenSecondOrderOnes,
    .cylinderMarginalConsistencyHasNoBellTypeObstruction ]

theorem two_sided_records_five_findings :
    twoSidedFindings.length = 5 := by
  rfl

inductive TwoSidedOpenObligation where
  | characterizeGluingUnderConditioningDemands
  | connectTheMassGateToNoSignallingConstraints
  | checkWhetherLocalTomographyAddsGatesBeyondMass
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

def twoSidedOpenObligations : List TwoSidedOpenObligation :=
  [ .characterizeGluingUnderConditioningDemands,
    .connectTheMassGateToNoSignallingConstraints,
    .checkWhetherLocalTomographyAddsGatesBeyondMass ]

theorem two_sided_keeps_three_open_obligations :
    twoSidedOpenObligations.length = 3 := by
  rfl

def twoSidedClaimBoundary : String :=
  "For set-function weights over ℚ on finite nonempty contexts: a pairwise generated composite weight with cylinder marginals mu and nu exists exactly when mu and nu are both pairwise generated and mu univ = nu univ. Mass conservation itself needs no grade assumption, and sufficiency is an explicit slice-and-junction construction, the arithmetic form of a transportation plan. This characterizes cylinder-marginal gluing only: it says nothing about conditioning, no-signalling on non-cylinder events, or local-tomography counts, where Bell-type obstructions may live, and the demand that composites be second order remains an input rather than a derivation. On empty contexts the mass gate alone is not sufficient and nothing is claimed. Nothing here derives complex amplitudes, a Hilbert carrier, the Born rule, or primitive-base semantics."

end QMClosure
